WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:03.660
My passionate idol activities,

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:07.380
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:10.930
So far on Aikatsu!

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:16.890
I'm Hoshimiya Ichigo, a third-year at the idol school Starlight Academy.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.370
We all use Aikatsu cards to do our idol activities.

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:26.120
Now that Christmas is over, the last big event of the year is finally here!

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:28.670
What do you associate with New Year's Eve?

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.170
New Year's soba, naturally!

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.650
I guess that works.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:33.680
And New Year's bento! {I'm not too attached to this}

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:35.860
That's New Year's Day.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.430
When it comes to idols and 
New Year's Eve, it has to be <i>that</i>. {this line is so Japanese}

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.180
That?

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.560
This.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:48.510
The 64th Annual Red-White Aikatsu Battle!

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:52.650
We're the PowaPowa Puririn 
cheer squad, Arisugawa Otome, {how to ouentai}

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.300
Kitaouji Sakura,

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:56.770
and Kamiya Shion!

00:00:56.770 --> 00:01:01.160
The Red-White Aikatsu Battle will start at 7:15pm on New Year's Eve.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:01.980
Please...

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.450
...tune in!

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:06.130
It's Otome-chan and them!{fucking tachi}

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:11.110
That's right! New Year's Eve means the national event, the Red-White Aikatsu Battle!

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:15.190
PowaPuri is doing the promotions for it this year. {is?}

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.830
I kinda want to watch it now that they just told me to.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:19.970
Yeah, yeah!

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:22.350
We'll be doing more than just watch...

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.470
We'll be in it.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:25.340
Right.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:37.610
The Red-White Aikatsu Battle is a paradise with idols everywhere!

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:41.240
I never got to participate because I always had a conflict, so I'm way excited!

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:43.180
I see.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:45.370
So you're here, Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:47.930
Seira-chan and Kii-chan!

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:53.390
Aoi-chan, isn't it awesome how there are so many idols here?

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:55.280
Yeah, it's something special!

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:59.550
Hoshimiya Ichigo, I still won't lose to you!

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.390
If you're <i>do</i>, then I'm <i>re</i>.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.760
If you're red, then I'm white!

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:10.650
Let's Aikatsu hard all the way to the end!

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.740
Yeah, let's rock this thing.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:17.660
<i>Something will definitely come to the surface today.</i>

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:21.950
<i>Let's see what the reason behind Dream Academy's sudden rise is.</i>

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:25.950
<i>The person pulling the strings is somewhere in this building.</i>

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:06.960
Next in line, this way please! {what}

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:12.650
This is the Red-White backstage I've dreamed about!

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:17.430
The first thing we do as a participant is an interview with the event organizers.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:23.440
Since there are so many participants, there's no time for them to meet everyone before the event.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:26.210
That's why we have these meetings today.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.840
Wow, Aoi. You sure know your stuff.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:34.760
I've always watched the Red-White Aikatsu Battle since I was a little girl!

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:36.040
I've studied up on it.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.670
Hoshimiya Ichigo-san.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.180
Kiriya Aoi-san.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:40.650
Shibuki Ran-san.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:41.660
Come on in.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:46.090
This is the first Red-White Aikatsu Battle for all three of you, right?

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:47.600
Yes!

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:54.020
The Red-White Aikatsu Battle is a traditional New Year's Eve event where idols Aikatsu against each other.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:56.830
I know!

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.860
It's been a dream of mine to be in one of these! {or something, this line was just weird}

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:03.240
It's a festival that only happens once a year, so Aikatsu your hearts out. {I feel like I use Aikatsu as a verb more than you do}

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:04.470
Okay!

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:07.550
Kiriya-san, nice to meet you.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:08.740
Nice to meet you too.

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:15.370
We'd like you to make an appearance as your character from that hit movie you starred in.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:16.530
Sure!

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:17.640
I'll do my best!

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:23.780
Shibuki-san, we'd like you to compete in the Fashion Corner.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:25.190
And there's someone else too...

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:27.090
Ah, there she is.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:30.350
Kazesawa Sora...

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:35.600
You'll be modeling alongside Kazesawa Sora-san, who recently started her own brand, Bohemian Sky. {first chan/san miss. also comma?}

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:37.700
Let's do our best, Ran-chan.

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:40.310
We'll put on a wonderful performance together.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:41.670
You got it.

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:43.690
Let's make this one great.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.790
So I'm doing the concert?

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:47.240
Yes.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.240
Sorry for the wait.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:54.250
Hoshimiya Ichigo, it's been a while since we've stood on stage together.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.730
Seira-chan!

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:58.240
Yay! I'm with Seira-chan!

00:05:58.240 --> 00:05:59.840
This is gonna be awesome!

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:04.820
I'm so excited that my girls get to participate in the Red-White! {pumped? stoked? moved? ugh?}{seemed fine to me}

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:06.720
Looks like this year will be a blast as well.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:07.710
Yeah, really.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:09.440
If you're <i>do</i>, then I'm <i>re</i>.

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:14.020
Seeing Ichigo-chan and Seira perform together at the Red-White makes me so happy.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:19.150
Both Otoshiro-san with her debut and Hoshimiya with her sudden return were huge this year.

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:23.520
It'll be a performance that encapsulates the year quite well. {I feel like there's a way to word this to make it super nice}{brings everything together?}

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:26.620
Let's do our best.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:28.260
Yeah, I won't lose.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:29.540
See you later.

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:37.890
<i>That right then... it couldn't have been...</i>

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:42.080
Aoi, Ran! How were your meetings?

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:43.910
Mine went well.

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:44.790
Mine too.

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:46.300
I can hardly wait!

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.220
Hurry! The special guest is here!

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:49.340
Okay!

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.270
Special guest?

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:53.120
Yeah.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:57.150
We have a super special guest this year, too! {ughhhhhh}

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.510
Let's go introduce ourselves!

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:01.860
Who's the guest?

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:04.110
This year's is one of the biggest names in enka!

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:09.660
It'll definitely be educational to see an industry veteran in person.

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:11.990
So this is even more Aikatsu.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:13.420
We have to be careful, though.

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:17.600
This year's guest, Nishijima Sabuko-sensei, is rumored to be really scary.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.790
What, the guest is Sabuko-sensei?!

00:07:19.790 --> 00:07:20.250
Yeah.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:22.130
Now I'm scared.

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:28.880
There's a rumor that Sabuko-sensei shoots lightning bolts at idols that greet her too quietly.

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:33.390
That's seriously special!

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:34.510
And also...

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:41.390
When she sees an idol give an uninspired performance, she'll storm into the dressing room in a fit of rage.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.270
That's some special intensity!

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.240
We have to greet her properly.

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:52.990
Yeah.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:53.950
L-Look!

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:59.220
It's Sabuko-sensei's truck!

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:00.910
How gaudy.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:04.040
It's huge!

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:07.980
There wasn't even a truck like this in America! {I feel like we have to do something to account for the amazing way she says AMERICA}{spell it aMErica}

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:09.910
Sabuko-sensei's amazing!

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:14.610
You see, Sabuko-sensei is famous for wearing huge clothing.

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:20.020
Which means there's a huge outfit in that truck.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:22.490
Yeah, there has to be!

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:24.190
I wonder what this year's outfit is.

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:33.350
What's that?!

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:34.450
A card?

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:37.680
Th-That isn't an Aikatsu card...

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:38.700
That's right.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:41.620
Sabuko-sensei!

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:44.460
This is an Enkatsu card, you see.

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:46.090
Enkatsu card?

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:48.560
Sensei, good work! {ewtgfsitobgnrf}{welcome? fuck I don't know}

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:50.960
Ah! Good work!

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:53.090
So there are even Enkatsu cards...

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:58.610
There were only whispers of their existence until now, but it looks like the rumor's been confirmed.

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:01.350
I never thought I'd get to see one with my own eyes...

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:04.230
To enka singers, cards are life itself.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:10.850
My elegant Enkatsu will light up this year's New Year's Eve.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:13.690
One... two!

00:09:15.670 --> 00:09:16.610
It's heavy!

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:19.240
If we don't hurry, we won't make it for the rehearsal!

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:21.580
Looks like they're having some trouble.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:23.550
Excuse me, Sabu-chan!

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:24.250
Huh?

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.020
Did you just call her Sabu-chan...

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:27.500
Somehow, it fits. {?}{that is accurate}

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:28.710
What is it?

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:31.540
We'll help!

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:38.260
Ai... katsu! Ai... katsu!

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:39.950
Is this really Aikatsu?

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:41.260
It's specifically not Aikatsu...

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:42.770
Oh right!

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:45.640
Enkatsu! Enkatsu!

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:47.650
What nice girls.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:50.520
En... katsu!

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:53.280
We made it.

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:56.510
I wonder what it'll look like on stage.

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:57.610
I can't wait!

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:58.160
Me too!

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:02.110
We probably should've prepared some sort of special outfit, too.

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:03.170
You mean a big one?

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:04.620
It doesn't have to be big...

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:09.040
It's just that, since it's the Red-White, it'd be nice to wear something different.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.170
You there.

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:12.880
Come with me.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:17.930
Good work there.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:21.300
Thank you for carrying my Enkatsu card.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.430
No problem!

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:27.030
Young idols usually shy away from me even when they're trying to introduce themselves.

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:28.890
They must think I'm scary.

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:30.950
But you were different.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:34.360
We just wanted to help, right?

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.250
Yeah.

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:36.820
Hoshimiya Ichigo. {Strawberry Starcastle!}

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:38.570
Kiriya Aoi. {Hollyhock Mistarrow!}

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:40.280
Shibuki Ran. {Orchid Purpleblow!}

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:42.830
You know about us?

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:46.660
Yes. You're the ones Mizuki-chan approved of, after all.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:53.670
Just earlier, Mizuki-chan came to my dressing room to tell me to treat her juniors well. {I normally hate doing "junior" for kouhai, but there might not be a shikata for this one}

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:56.460
Mizuki-san was here?

00:10:56.820 --> 00:10:58.080
Yeah.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:03.580
So Mizuki-san was in this building?

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:18.990
Maybe Mizuki-san's not here.

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:22.030
She should still be somewhere in these halls.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:24.930
<i>I haven't seen Mizuki-san in so long.</i>

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:30.290
<i>The last time I saw her was on stage at the Starlight Queen Cup.</i>

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:35.170
Right afterwards, Mizuki-san left Starlight Academy.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:37.910
I have so many things to ask her.

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:42.640
Like why she left Starlight Academy, and lots of other things!

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:46.540
Ichigo...

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:49.090
Let's split up and look for her!

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:10.830
I thought I'd see you tonight.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.330
Mizuki-san!

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:15.790
Welcome back, Ichigo.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:19.050
I'm a little late, but I wanted to say it in person.

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:23.010
Mizuki-san, I'm back!

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:26.010
Mizuki-san...

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:29.010
Long time no see.

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:35.270
Mizuki-san, I have so much to ask you...

00:12:35.670 --> 00:12:36.730
Of course you do.

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:42.170
We've heard next to nothing about you since you left Starlight Academy.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:45.030
Mizuki-san, what are you up to these days?

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:48.280
You see, I'm at Dream Academy right now.

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:51.040
At DreAca?!

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:54.040
However, I'm not a student.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:56.540
What do you mean?

00:12:57.310 --> 00:13:02.670
DreAca's founder, Headmistress Tiara, wasn't very familiar with the world of idols.

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:05.930
Because her background was in the IT industry? {........}

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.380
Yes.

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:14.430
She asked me if I would advise her on what kind of training idols should go through.

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:19.550
And at the same, I found something new I wanted to do.

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:21.690
That's why we entered this partnership.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:24.120
Something new to do?

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:25.820
Production.

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:27.200
I knew it.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:35.330
The days I spent with you girls in Tristar and STAR☆ANIS were brilliant ones.

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:42.300
But as your senpai, I wondered if I could've guided you better.

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:46.100
While I was thinking that, I got interested in production.

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:49.320
Mizuki-san, are you going to become a producer?

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:51.100
I don't know yet.

00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:55.800
All I can say is that I want to make Aikatsu better. {I guess anyone would get tired of using passionate that much}

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:57.460
I'm still the same as you.

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:00.610
That's why, even if I'm with DreAca, I'm your...

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:01.610
...friend!

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:04.050
Right?

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:13.700
Yes.

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:18.940
Ichigo, you're on stage with Seira-chan today, right?

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:19.630
Yes.

00:14:19.990 --> 00:14:21.630
Use these if you'd like.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:24.450
Thank you so much!

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:26.010
Whether you'll use them well...

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:28.140
...is up to me! I'll do my best!

00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:32.040
Don't tell Seira-chan and the others about me.

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:35.520
I'm only supposed to be DreAca's backstage advisor.

00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:36.880
Okay!

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:42.150
Mizuki-san, I'm really happy I got to talk to you!

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:46.650
There's one more thing I want to do.

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:50.660
I want not just to guide idols, but to make them.

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:52.660
Make... idols? {like Miku!}{I told you Seira was a robot}

00:14:56.300 --> 00:14:58.970
We'll bring smiles to the world together again some day.

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:00.540
Until then, let's work hard.

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:02.410
Okay!

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:09.550
Thanks for telling me Dream Academy's secret.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:15.180
Ex-Starlight Kanzaki Mizuki has defected to DreAca's side.

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:18.180
This'll be a big scandal!

00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:21.310
Wh-What are you...

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:24.440
Don't mess with the hard-working young'uns! {a computer with exactly zero harddrive space}

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:27.900
I can see to it that you never report again.

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:30.000
I'll back off for now.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.770
Just because of that reputation of yours. {because she's beautiful}

00:15:37.090 --> 00:15:38.830
Alright, everyone!

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:42.830
It's almost time for the Red-White Aikatsu Battle!

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:46.130
We have guests from all over the country in the venue today! {this is slightly less impressive when you remember that it takes like one hour to go anywhere in Japan}

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:50.470
The much-anticipated 64th Annual Red-White Aikatsu Battle!

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:54.300
We're all super looking forward to it!

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:58.350
The 64th Annual Red-White Aikatsu Battle

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:00.660
is finally under way!

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:08.110
Ah, it's Onee-chan!

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:14.490
Let's get straight to introducing the guest judges for this year's Red-White Aikatsu Battle!

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:19.920
From the morning serial drama <i>Ame-chan</i>, it's Ame-chan! {should we translate these} {either note, or use Sweet Girl/Sweets Girl/Sugar Girl}

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:20.990
Choo-choo! {eruighsofnaweoijfosehjgs}{I'm not even sure what this is supposed to be}

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:25.000
And from the noontime serial drama <i>Llama-chan</i>, it's Llama-chan!

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.500
Llama!

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:30.760
And finally, from the nighttime serial drama <i>Kuma-chan</i>, it's Kuma-chan!

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.520
Growl, rawr!

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:38.100
If you don't cheer for the red team, I'll get you!

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:49.310
Here we go! The white team's fashion show!

00:16:58.390 --> 00:16:59.760
Things are heating up.

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:00.290
Yeah!

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:01.990
They're all amazing!

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:03.290
Everyone's trying their best!

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:07.790
I never thought I'd participate in the Red-White so soon after debuting.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.700
Next up is this year's special guest!

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:13.050
It's time for Nishijima Sabuko-sensei's performance!

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:14.780
Sabuko-sensei?

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:17.300
Yeah, she's really nice!

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:21.060
Nishijima Sabuko-sensei, welcome aboard!

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:31.820
You can't even see her face...

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:33.440
Huge!

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:34.320
Huge...

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:35.930
It's huge!

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:37.200
Oh my.

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:51.590
Please listen to Nishijima Sabuko's "The Story of Little Sabuko". {you... added in a -chan. I don't even know what to do}

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:53.450
Isn't it too big?

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:56.940
Hoshimiya Ichigo, we can't let her outdo us!

00:17:56.940 --> 00:17:57.630
Yeah!

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:58.720
Seira!

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:00.850
Kii-chan, Sora-chan!

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:01.860
Kii!

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:05.070
Seira, I brought your clothes for today!

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:07.620
Your dress for today is this one!

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:09.380
The Rocking Bison Coord!

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:11.730
It's part of the trending Trend Collection. {fuck you Japan, because trending is the perfect word to use for hayatteru here}{it's fine. also get your own damn coords}

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:17.660
The cards I got were also part of the Trend Collection!

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:18.990
Trend Collection?

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:21.890
Here's what a Trend Collection is: {ooh, game mechanics}

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:27.120
Each of the brands makes clothing based on the latest trends.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:31.350
The theme is decided at the World Trend Conference.

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:39.360
Animal patterns were popular this winter, so each brand put out an animal-patterned dress.

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:41.140
I made one too.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:44.100
Kii, thank you!

00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:45.150
Sure!

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:47.480
With that outfit, take flight on the stage!

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:48.550
Alright.

00:18:48.550 --> 00:18:49.980
To the sky! {not haba nice day?}{or Fly high, need to match OP for this stuff}

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:56.560
It's time for the final stage of this year's Red-White Aikatsu Battle!

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:59.840
Ichigo-tan and Seira-tan bringing you KIRA☆Power!

00:21:47.050 --> 00:21:53.330
At the 64th Annual Red-White Aikatsu Battle, the time for us to part is nearly upon us.

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:56.580
Let's see what this year's result is.

00:21:56.900 --> 00:22:00.710
Arisugawa Otome-chan will announce the results!

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:05.470
The result of this year's Red-White Aikatsu Battle is...

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:08.920
...a tie! {isn't that like kissing your imouto?}

00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:12.220
Okay, everyone!

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:13.430
Happy New Year!

00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:15.810
See you next year!

00:22:17.470 --> 00:22:20.560
<i>That's right. Next year will be my true test.</i>

00:23:55.700 --> 00:23:57.700
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.850 --> 00:24:01.190
Now that the Red-White's over, so's the year!

00:24:01.190 --> 00:24:04.080
I get to go home and eat Mama's home cooking!

00:24:04.080 --> 00:24:06.240
Make sure you watch your weight this year, okay?

00:24:06.240 --> 00:24:07.500
Don't worry!

00:24:08.190 --> 00:24:09.840
Happy New Year!

00:24:10.840 --> 00:24:13.460
First thing in the new year is the lucky idol race! {I can never do these next episode preview things, and not just because there are no CCs... I had more trouble with them in all the other things I translated too}

00:24:13.460 --> 00:24:14.800
And what a prize!

00:24:14.800 --> 00:24:16.930
You'll be a Premium Constellation Dress representative! {there's definitely more than just the dress, but it's hard to hear clearly}

00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:19.180
What a big New Year's gift!

00:24:19.180 --> 00:24:20.390
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:20.390 --> 00:24:21.810
Lucky Idol!

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:23.690
Always passionate, idol activities!
